                                  </items>
                                </chunk>
                              </chunks>
                            </chunk>
                          </chunks>
                        </chunk>
                      </chunks>
                    </chunk>
                    <chunk name="param_input" index="4">
                      <items count="9">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Who does the heavy lifting of the sweep: the occlusion rays (and the raycast shortwave in MRT Solve) AND the view-factor geometry of every probe x polygon pair (the cos·area/r² term) ahead of them.
Auto: rays on Embree when its natives load, else the OpenCL GPU when a device answers, else the managed BVH; geometry on the GPU when one answers, else the CPU.
GPU: rays and geometry on the OpenCL GPU even where Embree loads, which pays off on the sweep's large ray batches; a fallback to the CPU is reported in the log and as a warning, never silent.
Embree: Embree rays, geometry on the CPU.
BVH: the managed BVH and CPU geometry — the same answer on every machine.
GPU geometry is float; measured within 2e-6 per view factor of the CPU's at Reference fidelity.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">7258c537-3e17-4369-8fce-8c3263009aa1</item>
