            <chunk name="Object" index="155">
              <items count="2">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">59e0b89a-e487-49f8-bab8-b5bab16be14c</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">08edf175-505f-4f10-99c1-46f479db2c9f</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Description</item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Purpose: UTCI at 1.8 m for one hour in Istanbul from a fully coupled microclimate simulation.
Fidelity: Engineering - coupled urbanMicroclimateFoam, not validated for this site. Cite: Kubilay et al., urbanMicroclimateFoam.
Method: Air, Building, Vegetation and Terrain regions with Timing Parameters from the EPW at a Calendar hour; MRT View Factors and MRT Solve.
Result: Mean UTCI per sensor with a legend; probed air temperature, wind, humidity, surface and tree temperatures.
Needs: Eddy3D Setup &gt; Fully-coupled multi-region CFD / HAM / RAD / VEG (urbanMicroclimateFoam), on BlueCFD, WSL or container. Runtime: hours.
Edit: Embedded building, tree and terrain meshes; weather file and Calendar hour.</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="2">
                    <chunk name="Attributes">
                      <items count="4">
                        <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
                          <X>14</X>
                          <Y>286</Y>
                          <W>420</W>
                          <H>280</H>
                        </item>
