            <chunk name="Object" index="159">
              <items count="3">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">410455b9-907c-4d4e-b4fd-9a61ab0e85c0</item>
                <item name="Lib" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">82b21a65-da8f-433c-93fb-f9814609e1d6</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Convert Units</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="4">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Convert values between the units Eddy3D works in — any unit into any other of the same kind, a single value or a whole hourly list. Temperature (°C, K, °F), speed (m/s, km/h, mph, kn), length, area, volume, pressure (Pa, hPa, inHg, psi), radiation (W/m², Btu/h·ft², kWh/m²), energy and power (kWh, Btu, kW, TR), mass, air flow (m³/s, cfm), rain rate, illuminance, humidity ratio (g/kg, gr/lb), enthalpy, U-value and conductivity, angle and time. EPW and every Eddy3D comfort input are in SI, OpenFOAM temperature fields are Kelvin: wire the values in, pick From and To.

Version 1.21.0.827</item>
